 
                                                  CONFIG Additional COMMAND


Checks for data of type IHEX, ASCII or reference data at a particular address.

Below is the syntax :
                 check 	-t {"IHEX"|"ASCII"|"REF"}  -addr address  -val value  [-l len]  [-n name] 

----------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES        |    DESCRIPTION
----------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -h           |    Specifies type IHEX, REF or ASCII. Mandatory switch.
   -ver         |    Address at which the data is checked. Mandatory switch.
   -?           |    Specifies the value to be checked. If the type is REF, value at address specified in -val is
                |    considered for comparison. Mandatory switch.
   -compensation|    For type IHEX and ASCII, length switch is an optional. If the type is REF then -l is a mandatory
                |    switch.
   -plv         |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.
   -overwrite   |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.
   -logfile     |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.
   -reset       |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.
   -byteorder   |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.
   -timestamp   |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.  
----------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

